1
00:00:13,513 --> 00:00:15,765
Do you believe in the force of gravity?

2
00:00:16,349 --> 00:00:19,269
We met for a reason.

3
00:00:19,352 --> 00:00:22,397
Why?

4
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:24,357
How could this happen?

5
00:00:24,441 --> 00:00:28,111
Why won't you let me die with Perla?

6
00:00:33,867 --> 00:00:35,785
I can't suppress my rage.

7
00:00:35,869 --> 00:00:37,954
We have a score to settle.

8
00:00:38,038 --> 00:00:40,874
Weather, meet your end.

9
00:00:47,380 --> 00:00:50,800
A man with no memories
might as well be dead.

10
00:02:22,809 --> 00:02:27,564
EPISODE 32: HEAVY FORECAST (3)

11
00:02:27,647 --> 00:02:28,565
Dumbass!

12
00:02:28,648 --> 00:02:30,275
Drive straight, idiot!

13
00:02:30,358 --> 00:02:32,777
This better not be on purpose.

14
00:02:32,861 --> 00:02:34,779
I can't even think about messing around!

15
00:02:34,863 --> 00:02:38,408
Look, it's trying to eat me!

16
00:02:39,701 --> 00:02:40,785
Weather…

17
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:41,828
What?

18
00:02:41,911 --> 00:02:45,165
I sense Weather's presence near Pucchi's!

19
00:02:45,957 --> 00:02:47,625
Are they together?

20
00:02:47,709 --> 00:02:51,713
I can't tell,
but they're near one another.

21
00:02:54,007 --> 00:02:54,924
Weather!

22
00:02:55,008 --> 00:02:58,511
What did you say? Kill you?

23
00:02:58,595 --> 00:03:01,180
- Yes.
- Don't mess with me!

24
00:03:01,264 --> 00:03:03,516
What is going on? Why do you say that?

25
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:06,811
In 1988,

26
00:03:06,895 --> 00:03:08,980
the same phenomenon struck my hometown.

27
00:03:09,063 --> 00:03:09,981
What?

28
00:03:10,064 --> 00:03:13,693
It seems that something deep within
my heart is wreaking this havoc.

29
00:03:14,277 --> 00:03:18,740
So your memories came back.

30
00:03:19,908 --> 00:03:22,452
Then fix this mess!

31
00:03:23,077 --> 00:03:25,204
I can't control this power.

32
00:03:25,788 --> 00:03:27,999
Kill me, and the Stand disappears.

33
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:33,379
I feel a sense of guilt
about turning people into snails,

34
00:03:33,463 --> 00:03:36,174
but I abhor my life.

35
00:03:36,758 --> 00:03:42,555
A part of me feels satisfied
to see this phenomenon.

36
00:03:43,056 --> 00:03:43,890
You…

37
00:03:47,518 --> 00:03:52,065
Jolyne better not be turning into a snail.

38
00:03:52,148 --> 00:03:54,025
Try not to move.

39
00:03:54,609 --> 00:03:56,778
I can't even begin to guess,

40
00:03:56,861 --> 00:04:01,866
but it's likely that touching the snails
triggers metamorphosis.

41
00:04:03,076 --> 00:04:03,910
Moreover,

42
00:04:04,410 --> 00:04:06,371
I need someone to finish me off.

43
00:04:07,121 --> 00:04:10,291
Stop with your bullshit.

44
00:04:10,375 --> 00:04:13,711
Tell me where Jolyne is, right now!

45
00:04:13,795 --> 00:04:16,339
I'll tell you after my score
with Pucchi is settled.

46
00:04:17,298 --> 00:04:20,885
Like I said, he is very close.

47
00:04:21,636 --> 00:04:24,013
W-What?

48
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:25,431
He's here.

49
00:04:25,515 --> 00:04:27,934
My sole purpose in life

50
00:04:28,810 --> 00:04:30,979
is to settle my score with him.

51
00:04:32,897 --> 00:04:34,190
I'm also doing this for F.F.

52
00:04:34,274 --> 00:04:39,195
I have to stop Pucchi
from using Jolyne's father's memory.

53
00:04:39,279 --> 00:04:40,863
It's time to put an end to everything.

54
00:04:40,947 --> 00:04:42,782
I will finish off Pucchi.

55
00:04:44,492 --> 00:04:46,828
Once I do, kill me.

56
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:47,870
Do you understand?

57
00:04:48,830 --> 00:04:49,914
All right.

58
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:52,166
I also owe him one for F.F., too.

59
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:53,334
I'll see you through.

60
00:04:53,918 --> 00:04:55,461
So where's the priest?

61
00:04:55,545 --> 00:04:57,046
North? Or south?

62
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:59,299
It's not even a matter of the direction.

63
00:04:59,382 --> 00:05:00,842
He's already here.

64
00:05:01,801 --> 00:05:04,137
He's within our 20-meter radius.

65
00:05:04,887 --> 00:05:09,100
He's not underground.
I checked with Diver Drive.

66
00:05:10,101 --> 00:05:12,228
Are you sure he's moving through
these swarms of snails

67
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:15,148
to close in on us?

68
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:19,485
Weather Forecast!

69
00:05:26,617 --> 00:05:28,536
There's no disruption in the air flow.

70
00:05:29,245 --> 00:05:32,832
Nothing is breathing or moving.

71
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:38,254
What about inside the cars, Weather?

72
00:06:10,328 --> 00:06:11,537
Weather!

73
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:19,712
I am painfully aware
of your control over the weather.

74
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:25,301
Every living thing, animals, and insects,
turns into snails in this phenomenon.

75
00:06:25,885 --> 00:06:28,679
Once I learned how the weather works,

76
00:06:30,098 --> 00:06:33,893
I no longer fear touching the snails!!

77
00:06:34,519 --> 00:06:36,062
I now know why it happens.

78
00:06:36,145 --> 00:06:39,982
When I extracted your memory in 1988,

79
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:44,737
I overcame this Stand,
though it almost cost me my life!

80
00:06:44,821 --> 00:06:45,988
You…

81
00:06:46,072 --> 00:06:48,616
Pucchi, you bastard!

82
00:06:56,332 --> 00:06:58,501
You are also finished.

83
00:06:59,001 --> 00:07:01,838
You should have served
your prison sentence

84
00:07:01,921 --> 00:07:06,384
instead of getting involved
with Jolyne and me.

85
00:07:06,467 --> 00:07:07,301
Dammit…

86
00:07:07,885 --> 00:07:08,970
Why?

87
00:07:09,053 --> 00:07:10,805
Why isn't Pucchi affected?

88
00:07:11,389 --> 00:07:13,266
How do these snails work?

89
00:07:13,349 --> 00:07:15,518
Tell me, Weather!

90
00:07:17,728 --> 00:07:19,730
This will do.

91
00:07:20,773 --> 00:07:25,862
If you are going to die, Weather,
I hope it takes a few more hours.

92
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:29,282
That's why I blasted your leg off.

93
00:07:29,866 --> 00:07:32,410
That should be enough time for your Stand

94
00:07:32,493 --> 00:07:37,623
to eliminate anyone who gets in my way.

95
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:41,836
The one who will help me get to heaven,

96
00:07:41,919 --> 00:07:46,674
it's none other than you, Weather.

97
00:07:53,431 --> 00:07:56,142
The new moon rises in three days.

98
00:07:56,225 --> 00:07:58,269
Then, everything will begin.

99
00:07:58,853 --> 00:08:01,731
The thing that The Green Baby sought

100
00:08:01,814 --> 00:08:06,736
and the heaven that Dio hoped to reach
is inside my body.

101
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:17,288
I submerged Diver Drive…

102
00:08:17,914 --> 00:08:19,081
into Weather's body!

103
00:08:19,665 --> 00:08:21,459
Weather Forecast!

104
00:08:27,882 --> 00:08:31,260
Grab hold of the priest, Weather!

105
00:08:31,344 --> 00:08:34,180
His Stand is inept at fighting!

106
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:38,309
Once you grab him, you can overpower
him with your gust of wind!

107
00:08:38,392 --> 00:08:41,354
Now, grab him! Don't let him get away!

108
00:08:48,361 --> 00:08:50,196
What?

109
00:08:51,781 --> 00:08:52,949
Weather!

110
00:08:53,991 --> 00:08:55,993
Damn it, why am I turning?

111
00:08:56,077 --> 00:08:58,329
I haven't touched any snails!

112
00:08:58,412 --> 00:08:59,372
Pucchi!

113
00:08:59,455 --> 00:09:01,499
What the hell did you do?

114
00:09:01,582 --> 00:09:03,376
Tell me!

115
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:05,044
It's subliminal.

116
00:09:06,420 --> 00:09:08,256
Like hidden words in a poster,

117
00:09:08,339 --> 00:09:11,342
indiscernible words
are incorporated in images.

118
00:09:11,425 --> 00:09:16,013
Or a single frame
is inserted into a film reel.

119
00:09:16,097 --> 00:09:18,975
Though imperceptible they may be,

120
00:09:19,058 --> 00:09:23,104
the subconscious retains that information.

121
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:26,566
That's the definition
of subliminal messaging in psychology.

122
00:09:26,649 --> 00:09:28,859
It's an effect on the subconscious.

123
00:09:29,443 --> 00:09:32,905
Subliminal messages easily enter the mind
and stimulate instinct

124
00:09:32,989 --> 00:09:34,907
more effectively than direct methods.

125
00:09:34,991 --> 00:09:39,370
They powerfully influence
and take over human behavior.

126
00:09:39,453 --> 00:09:42,873
Weather Forecast's rainbows

127
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:45,835
are sending subliminal messages
in the form of the weather.

128
00:09:45,918 --> 00:09:49,839
The image is seeping into the hearts
of everyone in the city.

129
00:09:50,423 --> 00:09:53,676
Are images of snails
hidden in the rainbows?

130
00:09:53,759 --> 00:09:56,470
Do rainbows stimulate primitive instincts?

131
00:09:57,054 --> 00:09:58,723
Anyone who sees the rainbow

132
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:01,976
starts to believe that
they are turning into a snail.

133
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:05,688
This strong belief forces the body
into metamorphosis.

134
00:10:05,771 --> 00:10:08,149
What? What did you just explain?

135
00:10:08,774 --> 00:10:10,526
This is the answer.

136
00:10:10,610 --> 00:10:13,904
It's the mechanism of
Weather Forecast's ability I sealed.

137
00:10:14,488 --> 00:10:18,117
My hometown was affected by his powers
long ago.

138
00:10:18,701 --> 00:10:21,871
When I saw a blind old woman
unaffected by the phenomenon,

139
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:25,541
I realized how his ability works.

140
00:10:25,625 --> 00:10:27,918
She was blind? That means…

141
00:10:28,002 --> 00:10:29,170
Weather,

142
00:10:29,253 --> 00:10:33,382
I don't need vision to see where you are.

143
00:10:33,466 --> 00:10:37,386
I've extracted my sight,
but I can sense you.

144
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,138
Let me tell you.

145
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:42,099
It's too late to close your eyes,
Anastasia.

146
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:46,979
Once the subliminal message settles
in your brain, you cannot undo its effect.

147
00:10:47,063 --> 00:10:51,651
This phenomenon will not end
until Weather dies.

148
00:10:54,278 --> 00:10:56,405
I'll take the other leg, for good measure.

149
00:11:00,826 --> 00:11:02,411
You will never stand again.

150
00:11:02,495 --> 00:11:03,871
Diver Drive!

151
00:11:03,954 --> 00:11:07,208
Don't let your rash feelings take over.

152
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:12,129
We must all get to heaven.

153
00:11:12,213 --> 00:11:17,009
My purpose can bring
all human beings to heaven.

154
00:11:17,093 --> 00:11:19,970
You are getting in my way.

155
00:11:20,054 --> 00:11:23,391
You're letting a few deaths dictate
the fate of the masses!

156
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:25,726
Domine quo vadis?

157
00:11:25,810 --> 00:11:29,355
You shall be crucified!

158
00:11:36,320 --> 00:11:38,697
What… just stabbed me?

159
00:11:41,200 --> 00:11:43,244
This is your doing, Weather.

160
00:11:43,327 --> 00:11:45,079
What are you doing?

161
00:11:45,162 --> 00:11:46,997
What is this sound?

162
00:11:47,081 --> 00:11:49,708
What are you scheming to do?

163
00:11:49,792 --> 00:11:54,463
This Weather Forecast ability
is something I can control.

164
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:59,218
I can take my time.
What counts is that I form them.

165
00:11:59,301 --> 00:12:01,429
They can be simple!

166
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:04,890
The blood was blown upwards,
then frozen with a cold draft.

167
00:12:05,516 --> 00:12:08,436
He's making spikes in the blood puddles.

168
00:12:08,519 --> 00:12:10,354
The priest can't see them!

169
00:12:10,438 --> 00:12:12,273
What will you choose?

170
00:12:12,356 --> 00:12:15,151
Yes, it's your choice to stay blind,

171
00:12:15,651 --> 00:12:20,072
but you may also choose to see
what's happening for yourself!

172
00:12:20,156 --> 00:12:22,575
Trip, and your life will end.

173
00:12:27,288 --> 00:12:30,708
I'm coming for you now.

174
00:12:35,254 --> 00:12:36,964
STAND NAME: PALE SNAKE
STAND MASTER: FATHER PUCCHI

175
00:12:39,383 --> 00:12:42,970
Pucchi, you have no way to escape.

176
00:12:43,053 --> 00:12:44,847
Will you restore your sight?

177
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:48,309
Do it. I'll reflect the rainbows
right into your face.

178
00:12:48,392 --> 00:12:52,313
Weather just has to grab Pucchi.

179
00:12:52,396 --> 00:12:55,024
Pale Snake is no match
for Weather Forecast.

180
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:57,651
Weather will win.

181
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:01,739
I knew you'd resist somehow.

182
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:06,368
No, you won't just let me leave.

183
00:13:06,869 --> 00:13:09,497
Not after regaining those memories.

184
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:11,457
And yet!

185
00:13:13,584 --> 00:13:14,877
Anastasia!

186
00:13:14,960 --> 00:13:17,546
Eyes are everywhere.

187
00:13:17,630 --> 00:13:19,298
I used them to get this far.

188
00:13:19,381 --> 00:13:22,092
Anastasia, do me a favor.

189
00:13:22,176 --> 00:13:25,012
Be my eyes.

190
00:13:25,596 --> 00:13:28,516
Tell me what you see.

191
00:13:28,599 --> 00:13:31,352
Tell me the dangers that surround me.

192
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:33,604
What is Weather doing?

193
00:13:35,523 --> 00:13:39,777
He used his spilled blood to make spikes
that protrude from the ground.

194
00:13:40,528 --> 00:13:42,821
Three spikes right behind you.

195
00:13:42,905 --> 00:13:45,574
Four more to your right.

196
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:47,535
I see.

197
00:13:47,618 --> 00:13:51,247
Will you guide me out of this spike trap?

198
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:53,457
Continue.

199
00:13:53,541 --> 00:13:55,876
Take three steps,
and six spikes lie ahead.

200
00:13:55,960 --> 00:13:58,337
Turn left.

201
00:14:01,131 --> 00:14:02,341
Weather.

202
00:14:02,424 --> 00:14:05,511
You were cursed from the moment
you were born.

203
00:14:06,804 --> 00:14:09,223
Stay down.

204
00:14:09,306 --> 00:14:13,394
Your life is fated for doom.
Nothing can save it.

205
00:14:14,311 --> 00:14:17,982
It would've been better
if you had lost your memories forever.

206
00:14:19,525 --> 00:14:22,027
Turn left and take five steps.

207
00:14:22,111 --> 00:14:24,280
Face right, and you are out.

208
00:14:24,363 --> 00:14:26,198
Okay. Five steps.

209
00:14:26,282 --> 00:14:28,158
That's right. Five more steps.

210
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:30,578
Also, I just noticed this.

211
00:14:30,661 --> 00:14:32,538
Since I can see it, I'll tell you.

212
00:14:33,163 --> 00:14:35,124
There's one more spike.

213
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:39,128
I didn't notice it until now
since I was looking down at the ground.

214
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:41,755
One of them pierced through your shoulder.

215
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:45,384
Weather is freezing your blood.

216
00:14:45,467 --> 00:14:48,345
Oh, too late.

217
00:14:50,514 --> 00:14:52,057
A cheap trick!

218
00:14:53,100 --> 00:14:54,768
It's not a trick.

219
00:14:54,852 --> 00:14:56,478
Weather is stronger than you.

220
00:14:56,562 --> 00:14:58,939
Weather is going to win!

221
00:15:00,941 --> 00:15:03,485
This wind pressure!

222
00:15:03,569 --> 00:15:07,698
I must get out of Weather's attack range!

223
00:15:08,532 --> 00:15:10,200
Just evade once.

224
00:15:10,784 --> 00:15:13,954
He just has enough strength left
for one attack!

225
00:15:16,290 --> 00:15:18,626
Take your own blood spikes!

226
00:15:19,126 --> 00:15:20,628
It's useless!

227
00:15:20,711 --> 00:15:23,505
Weather can dodge your throw easily!

228
00:15:23,589 --> 00:15:26,258
Yes, he will dodge.

229
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:28,552
When he does, the wind pressure
will shift its direction.

230
00:15:28,636 --> 00:15:30,220
That's my chance to escape!

231
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,725
You're mine now.

232
00:15:36,602 --> 00:15:38,395
I finally have you.

233
00:15:39,855 --> 00:15:42,191
He didn't dodge.

234
00:15:42,274 --> 00:15:44,485
Weather caught the priest
by freezing more blood!

235
00:15:47,154 --> 00:15:49,114
Weather has him in his range!

236
00:16:02,419 --> 00:16:03,671
Is he dead?

237
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:08,258
Let go, Weather.

238
00:16:08,842 --> 00:16:14,723
I had every chance to finish you off
inside Green Dolphin Street Prison.

239
00:16:14,807 --> 00:16:18,227
But… I hoped to save you one day.

240
00:16:18,310 --> 00:16:20,104
That's why I took your memory only.

241
00:16:20,688 --> 00:16:24,274
I'm not pleading for my life
to save my own skin.

242
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:27,611
Prime numbers.

243
00:16:27,695 --> 00:16:30,322
- I did it for you, my younger brother.
- Two,

244
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:31,240
Three,

245
00:16:31,323 --> 00:16:35,119
- It was for the ability to get to heaven.
- Five.

246
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:39,832
Someone must reach heaven one day.

247
00:16:39,915 --> 00:16:40,791
Seven.

248
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:44,211
- Don't do this, Weather.
- Eleven.

249
00:16:44,294 --> 00:16:47,214
- Stop trying to end your life and mine!
- Thirteen.

250
00:16:48,465 --> 00:16:49,466
Seventeen.

251
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:54,138
You do not realize your own evil.

252
00:16:54,888 --> 00:16:57,057
You are the worst form of evil.

253
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:59,893
- Nineteen.
- He's horrified.

254
00:16:59,977 --> 00:17:04,940
The priest's face is frozen with despair.

255
00:17:05,024 --> 00:17:06,025
Twenty-three.

256
00:17:06,108 --> 00:17:10,029
Stop this, Weather. You are wrong!

257
00:17:10,738 --> 00:17:12,990
You are nothing but a cursed man!

258
00:17:13,073 --> 00:17:15,617
- And yet, I kept you alive!
- You are finished now,

259
00:17:15,701 --> 00:17:17,578
Father Pucchi!

260
00:17:23,751 --> 00:17:25,294
What the hell are you doing?

261
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:28,213
I said I'll kill you if
you do anything suspicious!

262
00:17:28,297 --> 00:17:31,133
No! A dust storm suddenly started.

263
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:33,802
Something like a screw busted the tire!

264
00:17:33,886 --> 00:17:36,013
I lost control!

265
00:17:36,096 --> 00:17:37,431
He's close by.

266
00:17:37,514 --> 00:17:39,099
We are close to Weather!

267
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,267
The priest too!

268
00:17:40,934 --> 00:17:43,479
But something about the outside seems off.

269
00:17:44,063 --> 00:17:46,899
You're right I can't see well,

270
00:17:46,982 --> 00:17:48,901
but something is
sticking out of the ground.

271
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:50,611
Weather!

272
00:17:50,694 --> 00:17:54,656
I know you're close by.
Answer me, Weather!

273
00:17:57,284 --> 00:17:58,952
What the hell are these things?

274
00:17:59,536 --> 00:18:01,038
What happened here?

275
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:03,791
The priest is moving close to us.

276
00:18:04,374 --> 00:18:05,876
We are extremely close to him.

277
00:18:05,959 --> 00:18:09,671
We have to find Weather.
We need to find him as soon as we can.

278
00:18:09,755 --> 00:18:12,341
There's something horrific happening here.

279
00:18:12,424 --> 00:18:15,094
Did Weather cause this dust storm?

280
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:17,638
Hasn't the priest turned
into a snail by now?

281
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:18,806
I don't know.

282
00:18:18,889 --> 00:18:22,351
I just know that he's here.
Search for him!

283
00:18:27,439 --> 00:18:29,108
Jolyne, I saw someone.

284
00:18:29,191 --> 00:18:30,526
He's over this direction!

285
00:18:31,026 --> 00:18:34,530
I can't tell whether it was Pucchi or
Weather, but I definitely saw someone!

286
00:18:34,613 --> 00:18:37,282
Jolyne, the wind is dying.

287
00:18:37,908 --> 00:18:40,911
Also, my body is starting to
go back to normal.

288
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:43,622
Does this mean…

289
00:18:49,169 --> 00:18:51,130
Pucchi!

290
00:18:52,548 --> 00:18:53,841
No, Jolyne.

291
00:18:53,924 --> 00:18:57,302
We can't fully control
our bodies or Stands yet.

292
00:18:57,386 --> 00:19:00,472
We lack the speed
and strength to defeat him.

293
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:02,182
We have to find Weather first.

294
00:19:02,266 --> 00:19:04,560
Defeat the priest,
and we'll know where Weather is.

295
00:19:04,643 --> 00:19:07,020
Stone Ocean!

296
00:19:08,188 --> 00:19:09,398
Jolyne!

297
00:19:17,948 --> 00:19:19,491
- What?
- Weather!

298
00:19:20,492 --> 00:19:23,829
No one can catch up to me now.

299
00:19:23,912 --> 00:19:28,250
Spend your remaining days
with your family and loved ones.

300
00:19:28,333 --> 00:19:30,711
It's futile to come after me.

301
00:19:30,794 --> 00:19:32,921
I will win.

302
00:19:34,965 --> 00:19:36,633
Stop, Jolyne.

303
00:19:38,343 --> 00:19:39,344
Anastasia!

304
00:19:39,845 --> 00:19:42,181
This isn't the priest.

305
00:19:42,264 --> 00:19:44,892
The priest already left.

306
00:19:44,975 --> 00:19:45,976
What?

307
00:19:48,437 --> 00:19:50,189
This is a revelation.

308
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:53,984
That's not Pucchi either.
It's a visage of the past.

309
00:19:54,067 --> 00:19:56,069
This must be Pucchi's ability too.

310
00:19:57,571 --> 00:19:58,697
Versus!

311
00:19:59,198 --> 00:20:00,782
The priest

312
00:20:00,866 --> 00:20:04,036
left a disc in his head
during the dust storm.

313
00:20:05,579 --> 00:20:08,207
Pucchi's visage overlapped with his body.

314
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:11,668
This was the presence you sensed.

315
00:20:11,752 --> 00:20:13,629
The priest had already finished him off.

316
00:20:16,548 --> 00:20:17,966
This is a revelation.

317
00:20:19,134 --> 00:20:20,802
Fate had chosen me.

318
00:20:20,886 --> 00:20:26,975
- It is guiding me to heaven…
- …in three days' time.

319
00:20:27,059 --> 00:20:31,021
- If it hadn't, I would have been defeated…
- Do you believe in the force of gravity?

320
00:20:31,605 --> 00:20:34,233
You were drawn here by gravity.

321
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:36,860
Weather!

322
00:20:38,237 --> 00:20:40,239
I told you. It's a visage.

323
00:20:40,322 --> 00:20:47,246
- No one can catch up…
- …to me now…

324
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:50,624
I'm no longer a snail. What happened?

325
00:20:51,291 --> 00:20:52,960
Where's Weather, Anastasia?

326
00:20:53,043 --> 00:20:56,380
Where did Weather go?
Ermes, where's Weather?

327
00:20:57,047 --> 00:20:59,049
You don't sense his presence anymore?

328
00:21:00,175 --> 00:21:02,970
You don't know where he is?

329
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:07,975
Emporio!

330
00:21:13,981 --> 00:21:16,275
Ermes, call a doctor.

331
00:21:17,067 --> 00:21:19,861
- The doctors should be back to normal.
- Jolyne…

332
00:21:19,945 --> 00:21:21,822
- Emporio!
- Jolyne!

333
00:21:23,782 --> 00:21:25,867
The wind has stopped blowing.

334
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:34,710
The rainbows are gone, Jolyne.

335
00:21:41,508 --> 00:21:42,801
This can't be.

336
00:21:44,136 --> 00:21:48,140
Does this have something to do
with our car accident?

337
00:21:48,223 --> 00:21:51,518
Did this happen because we came?

338
00:21:53,812 --> 00:21:55,147
Listen, Jolyne.

339
00:21:55,814 --> 00:21:57,816
People say that I'm a cold-blooded killer.

340
00:21:58,608 --> 00:22:03,447
At least, the newspapers said so,
and I completely agree with it.

341
00:22:04,614 --> 00:22:08,785
When they asked me
if I would give my life for my parents,

342
00:22:08,869 --> 00:22:10,412
I answered no.

343
00:22:11,413 --> 00:22:13,707
I would still say the same.

344
00:22:14,416 --> 00:22:18,378
My parents can't move my heart.

345
00:22:18,462 --> 00:22:19,504
But…

346
00:22:20,255 --> 00:22:25,594
I will give my life for the people
who brought me back to life.

347
00:22:26,345 --> 00:22:28,263
Weather was one of these people.

348
00:22:34,978 --> 00:22:35,979
This disc…

349
00:22:37,397 --> 00:22:38,231
Right.

350
00:22:38,732 --> 00:22:41,568
When Weather got impaled by Pale Snake,

351
00:22:41,651 --> 00:22:43,695
he used his enemy's ability.

352
00:22:44,529 --> 00:22:47,991
He used Pale Snake
to seal his ability inside a disc.

353
00:22:49,534 --> 00:22:50,619
Jolyne…

354
00:22:51,578 --> 00:22:53,997
Weather left this for you.

355
00:23:00,003 --> 00:23:02,798
Weather came back to life
when he left the prison.

356
00:23:03,423 --> 00:23:05,008
This is the proof.

357
00:23:07,844 --> 00:23:10,764
He was truly happy the last few days.

358
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,975
Weather was already saved!

359
00:23:17,104 --> 00:23:18,105
Weather…

360
00:23:23,360 --> 00:23:24,611
I wish…

361
00:23:26,238 --> 00:23:29,157
I wish we could talk just one more time.

362
00:23:32,035 --> 00:23:36,623
I want to talk to you
in the warm breeze again.

363
00:23:46,007 --> 00:23:47,968
Subtitle translation by: Megumi Hunter
